FLAW IN THE ORIGINAL zeta_stationarity_enhanced.py
  The finite-difference shift leaves k1-k2 unchanged, so ∇J is identically
  zero when finite. Overflow, not a failed test, produced the 3/20 count.
  This script uses a genuine 2-D gradient of S_I = |J|^2 and does not
  insert zeros into J.

